Z||000000||KitKar||08-25-2000||11:01 PM||||Anyone know of an affordable way to ship a car from the San Francisco CA area to Phoenix AZ?<BR>I can't afford to spend more than $100 or $200<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||frontal lobe||08-26-2000||12:01 AM||||I don't know if there is an affordable way to get a car SHIPPED.  I was checking into bring a Miata from Naples, Florida to Milwaukee, Wisconsin.  Places that shipped it wanted about $800 for the 1400 mile trip.<P>There are services that will find a reliable person to DRIVE your car to your destination.  Those services are called "driveaways".  The company I contacted quoted me at $300, so I think with your shorter mileage you may come in at your price range with that.<P>You can find all sorts of companies that ship or driveaway at <A HREF="http://www.movecars.com." TARGET=_blank>www.movecars.com.</A> <P>Hope that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||08-26-2000||11:00 AM||||One way to see about getting a break on transporting is to make it clear that you are in no huge hurry. I got a break of about 30% when I let the trucking company know to get it to me when they can get it to me.  The company would much rather move it at a discount rate then to "deadhead" an empty spot on their transporter. Check it out.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
